<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 40,800 in October.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 40,800 in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for unemployment in October and average earnings in September.</p>
<p>(Previous estimates in brackets, minus denotes fall, data seasonally adjusted unless indicated)</p>
<p>   UNEMPLOYMENT			OCT	 SEPT  (SEPT PREL)</p>
<p>    Monthly change		  -40,800   -37,900  (-35,600)</p>
<p>    Rate (pct)			 7.2*	7.4	   (7.4)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj change    -126,500   n/a     (-72,700)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj rate (pct) 7.1	 7.5	   (7.5)</p>
<p>NOTE - Mkts forecast 25,000 October unemployment fall</p>
<p>    Unemployment level (million)     2.030     2.071     (2.073)</p>
<p>    Unemployment level unadj     1.977     2.104     (2.104)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 3m adj   -32,000   -26,500  (-25,700)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 6m	 -25,400   -19,300  (-18,900)</p>
<p>   AVERAGE EARNINGS		  SEPT	AUG    (AUG PREL)</p>
<p>    underlying yearly chng (pct) 4.0	 4.0	  (4.0)</p>
<p>    index (base 1990)		133.3     132.4     (132.3)</p>
<p>    actual yearly chng (pct)     4.1	 3.7	   (3.6)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p>    Production-- underlying	4.25	4.25	 (4.25)</p>
<p>		  -- actual	    4.3	 4.2	   (4.1)</p>
<p>  Manufacturing -- underlying  4.5	 4.5 (4.5)</p>
<p>		    -- actual	  4.6	 4.5	   (4.5)</p>
<p>  Services -- underlying	   3.75	3.75	 (3.75)</p>
<p>	     -- actual		 4.0	 3.5	   (3.5)</p>
<p>NOTE: Consensus forecast 4.0 pct for overall underlying a erage earnings.</p>
<p>  UNIT WAGE COSTS		  SEPT	AUGUST  (PREL AUG)</p>
<p>  Monthly change vs yr ago     5.4	 5.8	   (5.4)</p>
<p>  Index (base = 1990)	    114.9     114.8     (114.4)</p>
<p>  3-mth vs same yr/ago	   5.2	 5.1	   (4.5)</p>
<p>  Index (base = 1990)	    114.7     114.6     (114.0)</p>
<p>MANUFACTURING OVERTIME HOURS</p>
<p>  (million per week)	     8.67	8.48	 (8.14)</p>
<p>  Index (base = 1990)	    99.8	99.7	 (99.7)</p>
<p>MANUFACTURING EMPLOYMENT (GB)</p>
<p>  monthly change (April	 +13,000   -6,000	(unch)</p>
<p>  Average mthly change last 3m +4,000   +3,000    (+6,000)</p>
<p>  Quarterly change (Q3)	 +11,000   -13,000 (Q2)</p>
<p>OVERALL EMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>(THOUSANDS, S/ADJ)</p>
<p>  WORKFORCE IN EMPLOYMENT	Q2	  Q1</p>
<p>  LEVEL				25,908    25,821</p>
<p>  CHANGE				  +87	-121</p>
<p>  NO.S IN EMPLOYMENT LEVEL     22,205    22,081</p>
<p>			   CHANGE	 124	 -77</p>
<p>  JOB CENTRE VACANCIES	   OCTOBER   SEPT    (PREL SEPT)</p>
<p>  change			     9,300    16,600   (+16,600)</p>
<p>  level				262,900  253,600  (253,600)</p>
<p>  Avg 3m change		    10,900    11,600   (11,600)</p>
<p>*Lowest unemployment rate and level since February 1991.</p>
<p>The ONS said the number of long-term unemployed, out of work for a year or more, fell to the lowest level since October 1991.</p>
